---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HomeOpening from '../components/HomeOpening.astro';
import Credibility from '../components/Credibility.astro';
import { EDITION } from '../lib/brand';

/**
 * THE SPLASH. ONE OPENING.
 *
 * This page shipped with two, behind `?v=a` (the split composition: headline and instrument side by
 * side, benefits as a numbered rail) and `?v=b` (the register: a table of what you get and when,
 * beside four ruled columns naming the rungs of the scale). Dan chose the split on 2026-08-28, so
 * the register and its switcher are gone, `HomeOpening` renders unconditionally, and
 * `components/HomeRegister.astro` is deleted rather than left in the tree unreferenced. The same
 * decision was taken on the finish page the same day, where three endings came down to one.
 *
 * A STALE `/?v=b` STILL RENDERS THIS PAGE. Nothing reads `v` any more, so an unknown parameter is
 * simply ignored — which is what an old link in somebody's history needs. There is no redirect and
 * nothing to 404 on.
 *
 * ── THE ONE SWITCH THAT IS STILL OPEN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * ONE OPENING, ONE LOCKUP. Both questions this file used to hold are settled.
 *
 * The Register opening went on 2026-08-28; `HomeOpening` renders unconditionally. So did the logo
 * switch: Dan asked for the Airtable mark on the splash (*"just for visibility, reference,
 * credibility"*) and named two placements without choosing, so both were built behind `?logo=`.
 * Oleh chose the standing lockup. `EditionMark` has one placement now and `HomeOpening` renders it
 * itself, which is also how it stopped being in the page CORNER — it used to be a flex child of
 * `main` asking for the page's right edge, under the review chips, which is what Dan objected to
 * (*"I don't like the logo in the corner, it's too small and too much in the corner"*). It is a
 * column-mate of the score ladder instead.
 *
 * A stale `/?v=b` or `/?logo=a` in somebody's history renders the splash normally: nothing reads
 * either parameter any more.
 */
---

{/*
  THE SPLASH TURNS THE COMPACT FOOTER OFF AND RENDERS THE CREDIBILITY SECTION INSTEAD.
  Dan, 09:05: "this footer can stay there like this for the form, just not on the splash page."
  It is not a deletion: the same three names are on this page in more detail, with logos and links,
  which is what he asked for at 02:02 and what the one-line version was failing to do.
*/}
<Layout title={`${EDITION}: the survey`} footer={false}>
  <main>
    <HomeOpening />
    <Credibility />
  </main>
</Layout>

